nce is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $2{x}^{2}=(\\sqrt{2}x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{2}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-2{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(\\sqrt{2}x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250165 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186249905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250165 #edb/ref 1069 "q-114032" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250165 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250165 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-3{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250165 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4b8555c3-b26d-54b8-b47b-601c910c10ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250165 #edb/ref 1074 "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $3{x}^{2}=(\\sqrt{3}x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{3}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-3{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(\\sqrt{3}x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250167 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186249853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250167 #edb/ref 1069 "q-114035" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250167 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250167 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{1+5{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250167 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2983a03c-228c-5295-a88a-957cc5ef8213" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250167 #edb/ref 1074 "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $5{x}^{2}=(\\sqrt{5}x)^{2}.$\n\nThus, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{5}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1+5{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+(\\sqrt{5}x)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{5}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250175 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186249977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250175 #edb/ref 1069 "q-114053" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250175 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250175 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250175 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c9656774-7502-5500-b821-e655b8cd94a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250175 #edb/ref 1074 "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|x|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-1}}=\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{|\\sqrt{3}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3}x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\sqrt{3}x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{3}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{|\\sqrt{3}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3}x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{3}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330288 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(4x)}{4}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330288 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330288 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "26bff1d2-1a1f-5568-b606-c926ad4e222e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330460 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x)}{4}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330460 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330460 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "38f382b6-b9e0-5d37-bb15-bf2017958200" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331165 #edb/ref 1080 "4\\text{arcsec}(4x)+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331165 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331165 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "88b1a168-dccc-5c24-aa5c-58eef11e4b53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331179 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(16x)}{2}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331179 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331179 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8a671a08-acf6-51a4-a4b1-a79a1a8a1a19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331672 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(4x)}{4}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331672 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331672 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c1c62bda-b0cb-5477-843f-9e7f08c270e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186330288 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186330460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186331165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186331179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186331672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332279 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332279 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332279 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186331672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332279 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2ed515ce-b125-59ef-ba87-1982f7680cc3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332729 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186332279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332729 #edb/ref 1069 "q-49519" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332729 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332729 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int \\frac{1}{4|x|\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332729 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cd302e3c-b39d-509b-8801-010e64d93a57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186332729 #edb/ref 1074 "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{4|x|\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-1}}=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|4x|\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $4x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{4|x|\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|4x|\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(4x)}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377538 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377538 #edb/ref 1069 "q-351845" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377538 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377538 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{10}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377538 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4068a5d2-2d7d-5115-9e90-ed45feea5f4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377538 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{10}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{10}{9\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/9)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{1+(x/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{10}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{10}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{1+(x/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (3\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\frac{10}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377539 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377539 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377539 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186427994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377539 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8d0f7cff-e86b-56b3-9a00-cbb02d98343e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377540 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377540 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377540 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d90c6aca-5f52-581d-b9b7-53525c39db0b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427993 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427993 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427993 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "15391250-e023-5a04-9057-9658fe4de707" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427994 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186427994 #